.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_ACERT_ADD1_ATTR 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_ACERT_add1_attr ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_NID ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_OBJ ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_txt ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_delete_attr
.Nd X509_ACERT attribute functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509_acert.h
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_add1_attr
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fa "X509_ATTRIBUTE *attr"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_NID
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fa "int nid"
.Fa "int type"
.Fa "const void *bytes"
.Fa "int len"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_OBJ
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fa "const ASN1_OBJECT *obj"
.Fa "int type"
.Fa "const void *bytes"
.Fa "int len"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_txt
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fa "const char *attrname"
.Fa "int type"
.Fa "const unsigned char *bytes"
.Fa "int len"
.Fc
.Ft X509_ATTRIBUTE *
.Fo X509_ACERT_delete_attr
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fa "int loc"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_ACERT_add1_attr
adds a constructed X509_ATTRIBUTE
.Fa attr
to the existing X509_ACERT structure
.Fa x .
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_NID
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_OBJ
add an attribute of type
.Fa nid
or
.Fa obj
with a value of ASN1 type
.Fa type
constructed using
.Fa len
bytes from
.Fa bytes .
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_txt
adds an attribute of type
.Fa attrname
with a value of ASN1 type
.Fa type
constructed using
.Fa len
bytes from
.Fa bytes .
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_delete_attr
will delete the
.Fa loc Ns th
attribute from
.Fa x
and return a pointer to it or NULL if there are fewer than
.Fa loc
attributes contained in
.Fa x .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_ACERT_add1_attr ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_NID ,
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_OBJ
return 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_delete_attr
returns a
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
pointer on success or NULL on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr X509_ACERT_get_attr_count 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn X509_ACERT_add1_attr ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_NID ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_OBJ ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_add1_attr_by_txt
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_delete_attr
were added in OpenSSL 3.4.
